          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}60\\div4&=15\\\\60\\div6&=10\\\\60\\div10&=6\\end{align*}$$\nEach quotient is a whole number. Thus 60 is a common multiple of the package sizes, allowing a comparison of the same number of donuts using whole packages.",
